  "slug": "intestinal-liver-mice-0dd6",
  "summary": "New atlases and models, from PANGEA to CCGA and MOTET, tie large harmonized omics cohorts to mutational processes, subtypes and survival.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is harmonizing large molecular datasets into reference resources, then extracting structure that links to outcome. PANGEA remaps 12.6M cells into a 32-type, 165-subtype hierarchy spanning 160 diseases; a 1,824-tumor lung RNA-seq cohort defines nine transcriptional clusters tied to histology, genetics, immunity and survival; CCGA harmonizes exomes from 667 canine tumor-normal pairs and reports 39 drivers. Preprints add modeling layers: MOTET jointly infers SBS, DBS and ID processes across 2,583 PCAWG genomes, EAGLE-MUT learns somatic mutation probabilities from sequence, and SNOWS and EvoSurv build survival-informed mutational and evolutionary representations. SNOWS raises C-index from 0.691 to 0.712 on CGGA transfer. CellChat Hotspot adds targeted filtering to communication inference.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-17"
}
